# secrets.env for cms_pilot: copy this file to secrets.env next to it (git-ignored)
# and fill it in. For GitHub runs, paste the same block into the GitHub
# Environment's SECRETS_ENV secret.
#
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored. Values are taken literally:
# no quotes needed. Logins aren't secret, but keeping them with their passwords
# means one paste per deployment.
#
# Every login below is an HRMS employee code (or the admin username) on the
# 2.12.1 password sign-in, not an email. Check that each one can sign in to the
# employee UI before the first run: the suite treats a refused login as
# "persona not available" and skips the tests that need it.

# ── Admin ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Signs in to the configurator (Management mode) and gets the API token most
# setup steps use. Needs: the state-level admin roles the configurator accepts
# (on a stock deployment this is ADMIN with SUPERUSER), at ROOT_TENANT.
# Example: ADMIN
# (ADMIN_USER / ADMIN_PASSWORD are accepted as deprecated aliases.)
DIGIT_USERNAME=
DIGIT_PASSWORD=

# ── GRO: assigns complaints ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Drives ASSIGN in lifecycle seeding and the PGR workflow specs.
# Needs:
#   - role GRO
#   - an HRMS employee record on DIGIT_TENANT (a login alone is not enough; an
#     admin with no HRMS record fails ASSIGN with DEPARTMENT_NOT_FOUND)
#   - a department that owns at least one complaint type (the suite files its
#     seed complaints with a type from that department)
# Example: GRO_PILOT, role GRO, department ROADS, jurisdiction the whole tenant.
GRO_USER=
GRO_PASSWORD=

# ── LME / employee: works the complaint ────────────────────────────────────────
# Takes action on assigned complaints (resolve, escalate) and drives the
# employee inbox and details specs.
# Needs:
#   - role PGR_LME (+ GRO if it should also see the assignment inbox)
#   - an HRMS employee record in the SAME department as the GRO above
#   - a jurisdiction that contains the seeded complaint's ward exactly (PGR does
#     not expand a parent boundary to its wards), or role SUPERVISOR, which sees
#     every ward
# Example: LME_PILOT, roles PGR_LME + GRO + SUPERVISOR, department ROADS.
EMPLOYEE_USER=
EMPLOYEE_PASSWORD=
# Only if this employee signs in at a different tenant from DIGIT_TENANT.
# EMPLOYEE_TENANT=

# ── City admin (optional) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by citizen/full-complaint-lifecycle-ui and specs/pgr-postal-code to act on
# a complaint from the employee UI. Needs: an employee whose login tenant equals
# the complaint's tenant (DIGIT_TENANT), with GRO + PGR_LME. Without it, those
# specs skip.
# The session checks (scope session-checks) also use it for the workflow pages:
# the inbox's "Open in new tab" (SEC/018–020) and a complaint's attachments and
# receipt (SEC/008). Give it the CMS roles; its HRMS department still filters its
# inbox (those checks file a complaint of its department). SEC/020 logs it out,
# which ends any manual session on it. It must not be DIGIT_USERNAME.
# Example: an HRMS employee at DIGIT_TENANT with GRO + PGR_LME + SUPERVISOR.
CITY_ADMIN_USER=
CITY_ADMIN_PASS=

# ── Ward-scoped CSR (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used by api/boundary-jurisdiction-496: a CSR must only see boundaries inside
# its own jurisdiction. Needs: role CSR, an HRMS record whose jurisdiction is ONE
# ward (below the top of the boundary hierarchy). Without it, that spec skips.
# Example: CSR_WARD1, role CSR, jurisdiction one ward of the tenant.
WARD_CSR_USER=
WARD_CSR_PASSWORD=
# The ward code that CSR is limited to, and wards it must NOT see (comma-separated).
# WARD_CSR_BOUNDARY=
# FORBIDDEN_WARDS=

# ── Extra candidates ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# More employee logins persona discovery may try, as user:password pairs,
# comma-separated (a password cannot contain "," or ":"). Example:
#   PERSONA_CANDIDATES=EMP001:pass1,EMP002:pass2
#
# The session and file-access checks (scope session-checks) also take their
# users from here: they need 2 accounts besides the admin — employees who can
# sign in (role EMPLOYEE). Accounts whose HRMS department owns a complaint type
# are picked first (then PGR roles), because the inbox checks file a complaint
# of user A's own department so that it shows in A's inbox. They are used on the employee UI
# and the configurator, and are signed in and out repeatedly, so any manual
# session on them is ended. (Citizens are created fresh by each test.)
PERSONA_CANDIDATES=

# ── Citizen OTP ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The fixed 6-digit citizen OTP, used when config.env sets no OTP_SINK_URL.
FIXED_OTP=
